# HanuOTP dark-launch env vars (phase 1) and shared auth secret
#
# Add real values to your secret store (Vercel project settings / local
# .env.local). None of these are NEXT_PUBLIC_ — they must never reach the
# browser bundle.
#
# HANUOTP_API_KEY is only used by the uncalled /api/hanu-auth/* routes.
# AUTH_HMAC_SECRET is also required by the active /api/email-auth/* routes.
# See /hanuotp-integration-plan.md for HanuOTP integration status.

# The exact HanuOTP endpoint from your account. Code defaults to
# https://api.hanuotp.in/sms-otp.php if this is unset — only set it here if
# you want to point at a different/mock endpoint during testing.
# HANUOTP_BASE_URL=https://api.hanuotp.in/sms-otp.php

# Your HanuOTP API key. Use a ROTATED key — the one shared earlier in chat
# should be treated as compromised and not used here.
HANUOTP_API_KEY=

# Any new random 32+ byte secret, separate from Firebase credentials. Signs
# email OTP hashes and HanuOTP OTP/session hashes. Generate one with, e.g.:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
AUTH_HMAC_SECRET=
